 "descripcion": "In 1300, most of the village ale was brewed by women at home. A day with Agnes, the brewster.\n\nPart 2: {when_next}.\nWhat does the green branch mean?\n\n#history #medieval #middleages #historyfacts #shorts",
 "lineas": [
  {
   "texto": "You wake up in 1300, in the house of the village brewster.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "This is Agnes. She's thirty-four, and half the village drinks her ale.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "Her ale keeps only a few days, so she brews almost every week.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "Your jobs: soak the barley, dry the sprouts, grind the malt.",
   "pausa": 0.7
  },
  {
   "texto": "By noon, the mash is steaming in her big pot.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "Then Agnes ties a green branch to a pole by the door.",
   "pausa": 0.6
  },
  {
   "texto": "Every neighbour knows what it means.",
   "pausa": 0.8
  },
  {
   "texto": "What does the branch say? Part two, {when_next}.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  }
 ],
